# Docs/ is mostly prose and certification evidence, but Dockerfile.playwright
# copies it and three of its files are runtime inputs: the RAG golden queries,
# the source contract, and the crawler selector gate config, all of which are
# resolved by relative path from src/. Excluding the whole tree made
# `COPY Docs/` fail with `"/Docs": not found`, which broke the text relay
# pipeline daily. Exclude the heavy subtrees and keep what is read at runtime.
#
# Docs/robots/ is a fourth runtime input, and it belongs to the plain Dockerfile
# rather than the Playwright one: the source inventory job and the crawler
# compliance check both read their per-host policies from a relative path. It is
# listed explicitly because a directory name is case-sensitive on Linux, and the
# code used to spell it `docs/robots` -- which resolves on macOS and not in the
# container, leaving every host unreachable and no policy enforced.
Docs/*
!Docs/references/
!Docs/robots/
Docs/certification/
Docs/incident-evidence/
.claude/
.antigravitycli/
.gemini/
